Something else.  This is a request for reactions, to see whether 
there is/would be community support for a successor to nethack 
"the way I'd make it."  

I have a roguelike engine mostly written already.  It's advanced 
enough in design to easily support a nethack successor (or something 
even more complex) and modular enough that you could make nearly 
arbitrary patches that *NEVER* interfere with each other.  I am 
inordinately pleased with it.

I'll be making a game on top of it, of course. 

My question here was more about whether it's worth my time and effort
to make that game explicitly a nethack successor (copy most of the 
monster and item lists, player races and classes, claustrophobic 
23x79 dungeon levels, copy features like Vlad's tower and Fort Ludios 
and Rodney, make it a Fetch-The-Amulet-of-Yendor Quest with a vibrating 
square and elemental planes, etc......).  

I could do that - modulo a few changes, as outlined, that I'd make 
because, well, it's mine and I consider copying those things which 
I consider "bad behavior" or "bad design" into my game to be 
dealbreakers, things that I would never do. 

Alternatively, I could make a completely different game and let the 
nethack community continue to wait for the next version from the 
devteam built on the devteam's extant codebase.  

